  "summary": "New preprints pair sequence-to-function predictors with eQTL and ancestry-aware analyses to resolve context-specific regulatory variant effects at disease loci.",
  "synthesis": "The common thread is resolving how regulatory variants act in specific cellular and genetic contexts. AlphaGenome 2 predicts cell-type-specific regulatory activity and variant effects from 1-Mb sequence, while ChromBPNet models across 17 hematopoietic cell types score 302,830 variants and show lineage-structured accessibility effects. Empirical work shows ancestry shapes allele-specific expression in admixed whole blood, with 52 ancestry-associated loci replicating. Applications to disease include CAS-X, which integrates fine-mapped eQTLs across five metabolic tissues for type 2 diabetes effector genes, and PrediXSKAT, which weights rare coding variants by predicted cis-regulated expression. The endometriosis study shows cell-state prioritization depends on marker definition and donor structure. A Mendelian randomization study of midkine in pancreatic cancer is more loosely connected.",
  "synthesis_model": "claude-sonnet-5-5",
  "synthesized_on": "2026-11-20"
}
